{"answerable":true,"answer":"You must be able to show records for the current day plus the preceding 56 days whenever an authorised control officer asks.

- **Analogue tachograph:** carry your record sheets for the current day and the preceding 56 days, your driver card if you hold one, and any manual records and printouts from that same period.
- **Digital tachograph:** carry your driver card and any manual records and printouts from the current day and the preceding 56 days. If you drove a vehicle with an analogue tachograph during that period, also carry the record sheets for it.","citations":[{"node_id":"165/2014:art36(1)","quote":"he shall be able to produce, whenever an authorised control officer so requests:"},{"node_id":"165/2014:art36(1)(i)","quote":"the record sheets for the current day and the preceding 56 days;"},{"node_id":"165/2014:art36(1)(ii)","quote":"the driver card, if one is held"},{"node_id":"165/2014:art36(1)(iii)","quote":"any manual records and printouts made during the current day and the preceding 56 days."},{"node_id":"165/2014:art36(2)(i)","quote":"his driver card,"},{"node_id":"165/2014:art36(2)(ii)","quote":"any manual records and printouts made during the current day and the preceding 56 days,"},{"node_id":"165/2014:art36(2)(iii)","quote":"the record sheets corresponding to the same period as that referred to in point (ii) during which he drove a vehicle fitted with an analogue tachograph."}]}

