verdict.answer:
Most likely not. Regulation 561/2006, which sets the driving time limits (for example 9 hours a day), does not apply to your truck if all of these conditions are met:
- the vehicle or combination is 7,5 tonnes maximum permissible mass or less (your 6 tonnes qualifies);
- it carries materials, equipment or machinery you use in your own work, such as your carpentry tools;
- you stay within a 100 km radius of your company's base (80 km is fine);
- driving is not your main activity;
- the transport is not done for hire or reward.
If any one of these conditions fails, the normal driving time rules apply. Examples would be going beyond 100 km or carrying goods for others for payment.
An older Commission note from 2007 describes a different exemption under Article 13(1)(d). That exemption was limited to a 50 km radius and only applied if your Member State chose to grant it. The current Regulation replaces it: the 100 km exclusion in Article 3 applies directly and does not depend on a national decision.
